  "question": {
    "text": "The resistance per centimeter of a meter bridge wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> resistance in left gap. Balancing length from left end is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> resistance in right gap. Now the wire is replaced by another wire of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></math> resistance per centimeter. The new balancing length for same settings will be at"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0068_d3f972132676.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 164px;\"/></p><p>For first case:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> ... (i)</p><p>For second case:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><msub><mo>'</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> ... (ii)</p><p>From (i) and (ii), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><msub><mo>'</mo><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><msub><mo>'</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mstyle></mfrac></math> also total length is constant.</p><p>Therefore, balance length doesn't change and </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><msub><mo>'</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>"
  }
}